<Base title="About Sunnah Tools" description="Who builds Sunnah Tools, how our Islamic calculators work, and the limits of calculated prayer times, Hijri dates and Zakat estimates.">
<section class="content">
 <h1>About Sunnah Tools</h1>
 <p>Sunnah Tools brings together prayer times, Islamic calendars, Zakat calculators and everyday worship planners in one place.</p>
 <h2>How the calculations work</h2>
 <p>Most calculations run in your browser. Prayer-time features use recognised astronomical methods, including configurable Fajr and Asr conventions; location searches use the GeoNames city directory. Hijri conversions use the Umm al-Qura calendar convention, and money tools explain how entered amounts are calculated.</p>
 <p>Calculated prayer times, religious dates and financial estimates can differ from the guidance used in your community. Each tool explains its method and where a result may need checking.</p>
 <h2>When to check locally</h2>
 <p>Islamic months may begin on different dates due to regional moon sightings. Local mosque prayer timetables may use different parameters or congregation times. Zakat, Fitrana and pilgrimage questions can depend on the user's circumstances and school of thought. We therefore present estimates and link to further references where possible, rather than claiming universal authority.</p>
 <h2>Advertising</h2>
 <p>Advertising may help support the website. Any adverts are clearly labelled and kept separate from calculations and religious guidance.</p>
 <h2>Found a problem?</h2>
 <p>If a result looks wrong or something is difficult to use, let us know through <a href="https://github.com/omairarshad/sunnah-tools/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the project issue tracker</a>. Please avoid submitting private financial or health details there. Please include the tool name and what you expected to see.</p>
 <p>Explore the <a href="/guides/prayer-time-methods/">prayer-time methodology guide</a> and <a href="/guides/ramadan-dates-and-timetables/">Ramadan date and timetable guide</a> for a closer look at the limitations of our tools.</p>
 <p><a href="/#tools">← Browse all tools</a></p>
